  "id": "cf",
  "term": "CF",
  "definition": "CF, or compassion fatigue, is a form of emotional and physical exhaustion that can develop after ongoing empathic involvement with seriously ill or traumatized people. In this source, it is also described as affecting a clinician’s beliefs and sense of professional identity, and as part of the broader “cost of caring” alongside secondary traumatic stress and vicarious trauma.",
